.TH RESET 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
reset \- restore a usable terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reset
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Reset
sets cooked and echo modes, turns off raw input, and turns on newline
translation. This is most useful after a program dies leaving a terminal
in a funny state.
.PP
On maux it also sends the terminal-reset escape sequence, clearing
display attributes, clearing the body and homing the cursor.
There is no terminal database lookup and no tset option language.
.PP
If a program has left input without echo, the command may still be typed
even though the characters are not visible.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/RESET  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
stty(1), vidmode(1), vi(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is always 0; recovery is best-effort.
.SH BUGS
The command uses standard output. If redirected, it writes the reset escape bytes there rather than resetting the console.
